There is hereby created the DeKalb County Women's Commission ("commission"). The commission shall advise and make recommendations to the board of commissioners, chief executive officer, chief operating officer, and department directors on issues pertaining to the wellbeing and advancement of women in DeKalb County.
The board of commissioners and the CEO shall each have the ability to annually assign to the commission topic(s) of study and discussion, on which the commission shall report at least annually to the board during a committee of the whole meeting as requested. Policy and legislative topics to be addressed may include, but are not limited to:
(a) Developing programs to identify and address disparities in healthcare;
(b) Developing programs to address wage inequity and employment issues;
(c) Developing programs to identify and address safety and security issues across communities and industries;
(d) Developing community-based programs to enhance the quality of life for women in DeKalb County;
(e) Developing programs to assist women and women's organizations in accessing federal, state, and local funding opportunities; and
(f) Identifying areas in which additional study would benefit women in DeKalb County.
(Ord. No. 2025-1606, Pt. I, 12-16-25)

